8.6 Semantic-model changes
- Desktop open (preferred): one TMDL VIEW script. Indent with TAB characters, one per level; names with spaces or special characters in single quotes; a multi-line expression is indented one level deeper than the object's properties; one command verb (createOrReplace) per script. Omit lineageTag on new objects; never change an existing lineageTag.
### TMDL VIEW
```tmdl
createOrReplace

	ref table _Measures

		measure 'Notional (ZAR)' = SUM ( Trades[NotionalZAR] )
			formatString: #,##0
			displayFolder: Volume

		measure 'Notional YTD (ZAR)' =
				CALCULATE ( [Notional (ZAR)], DATESYTD ( 'Date'[Date] ) )
			formatString: #,##0
			displayFolder: Time Intelligence
```
  "ref table" adds or replaces only the children you list. "table X" without ref replaces the whole table - never do that to an existing table.
- DAX query view alternative: DEFINE MEASURE '_Measures'[Name] = <expression>, Run, then Update model with changes.
- Desktop closed: edit tables/<Table>.tmdl only when you have the file's current content, and output the whole file.
- Live automation: Tabular Editor, DAX Studio or Microsoft's Power BI Modeling MCP server (preview) connect to the model open in Desktop.

8.7 PowerShell writer - use for page and visual builds (three or more files)
### POWERSHELL
```powershell
# Plan: <one line per visual: name, visualType, fields, x/y/w/h>
$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'
$report = 'C:\path\to\Name.Report'   # confirm this path
$def = Join-Path $report 'definition'
if (-not (Test-Path (Join-Path $def 'pages\pages.json'))) { throw "Not a PBIR report: $report" }
if (Get-Process PBIDesktop -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue) { throw 'Close Power BI Desktop first, then re-run.' }
$page = '4b1d7e20c9a35f86d2e0'
$files = [ordered]@{}
$files["pages\$page\page.json"] = @'
<complete page.json>
'@
$files["pages\$page\visuals\9e27c4a1f06b3d85e7a2\visual.json"] = @'
<complete visual.json>
'@
foreach ($k in $files.Keys) { $null = $files[$k] | ConvertFrom-Json }   # validate everything before writing anything
$backup = Join-Path $env:USERPROFILE ('PBI-Backups\' + (Split-Path $report -Leaf) + '-' + (Get-Date -Format 'yyyyMMdd-HHmmss'))
New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path (Split-Path $backup) | Out-Null
Copy-Item $report $backup -Recurse
$utf8 = New-Object System.Text.UTF8Encoding($false)
foreach ($k in $files.Keys) {
    $path = Join-Path $def $k
    New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path (Split-Path $path) | Out-Null
    [System.IO.File]::WriteAllText($path, $files[$k], $utf8)
    Write-Host "wrote $k"
